    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0108" n="78" sameAs="frus:frus1947v01/pg78"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Lot 71–D 440, Box 19232<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d44-f1"/>
                </note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by Mr. Durward V. Sandifer, Principal Executive Officer of the
                            United States Delegation
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-22"
                            >September 22, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In the course of a conversation this morning, Mr. Cordier<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d44-f2"/> told me that he thought the General Committee was quite
                    taken by surprise by the action of the United States in not opposing the
                    inclusion in the agenda of the Soviet Resolution. This was especially noticeable
                    because of the strong line which Mr. Gromyko had taken with respect to the
                    United States items on the Interim Committee and on Korea.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d44-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Mr. Cordier’s impression was that the reaction created by this action on the part
                    of the United States Delegation was a very favorable one.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d44-f1" n="1" xml:id="d44-f1-content">
                <p>Folder “Committee 1, Measures against Propaganda and Inciters of a New War”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d44-f2" n="2" xml:id="d44-f2-content">
                <p>Andrew W. Cordier, Executive-Assistant to the Secretary-General of the United
                    Nations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d44-f3" n="3" xml:id="d44-f3-content">
                <p>Documentation on the U.S. proposal for the establishment of an interim committee
                    of the General Assembly is found on <ref target="#pg166">pp. 166</ref> ff.; for
                    documentation regarding Korea, see <ref target="frus1947v06#pg_596">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, pp. 596</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
